Place @pears{8%medium}(cored and diced), @water{1%cup}, @ground cinnamon{1/2%tsp}, @ground nutmeg{1/4%tsp} and @ground cardamom{1/4%tsp} in the #slow cooker{}.

Cook on HIGH ~{3-4%hours} or LOW for ~{6-8%hours}.

For a chunky sauce, simply mash with a #potato masher{}, leaving large pieces here and there.

For a smooth sauce, let cool slightly, then work in batches to puree in a #blender{}. (Alternatively, you can use an #immersion blender{} to puree.)

Eat warm or cold! Store the finished pear sauce mixture in #pint jars{} or an airtight container in the fridge 4-5 days. Pear sauce can also be frozen up to 2 months. Thaw in the refrigerator before eating.

> No need to peel the pears.